# id: SEAM-zero-unbounded
# blinds: the bound on consecutive zero returns
# covering-lane: cpp-test
# expect: killed
# control-lane: cpp-build
# expect-control: alive
#
# A LIVENESS defect, and the reason the seam test's harness caps its own call
# count. Unpatched, WriteFully gives up after kMaxConsecutiveZeroWrites;
# patched, it retries forever. Without the harness cap this patch would HANG the
# lane rather than redden it, and a lane that hangs while checking a liveness
# property reports nothing at all -- so the cap is what makes this induction
# possible, not a convenience.
#
# The patch removes the `zeros` counter entirely, not just the bound. The first
# version removed only the bound and left the counter set-but-never-read, which
# -Wextra -Werror rejects -- so the tree did not compile and the control lane
# reported BROKEN instead of a kill. That is the control doing its job for the
# second time in this catalogue, and the reason every patch here carries one.
#
# NOT A CATALOGUE MUTANT. DESIGN-B1 section 14.2 records "Mutants: none" for
# B1.2b, and that is a statement about the BM catalogue: PosixEnv is outside the
# fault matrix, so it gets no BM number. But the standing rule is that no gate
# counts until its failure has been induced and observed, and B1.2b's gates are
# the three seam tests. This patch is that induction, made repeatable rather
# than performed once by hand -- there is no CI here, so an induction nobody can
# re-run is an induction that decays into a sentence in a commit message.
--- a/engine-cpp/src/env/posix/posix_raw.cc	2026-08-24 17:19:58
+++ b/engine-cpp/src/env/posix/posix_raw.cc	2026-08-24 17:19:58
@@ -14,7 +14,6 @@
 
 Status WriteFully(int fd, const char* data, std::size_t n, RawWriteFn raw) {
   std::size_t done = 0;
-  int zeros = 0;
   while (done < n) {
     const ssize_t w = raw(fd, data + done, n - done);
     if (w < 0) {
@@ -22,13 +21,8 @@
       return Status::IoError("write: errno " + std::to_string(errno));
     }
     if (w == 0) {
-      if (++zeros >= kMaxConsecutiveZeroWrites) {
-        return Status::IoError("write returned 0 " +
-                               std::to_string(zeros) + " times without an error");
-      }
-      continue;
+      continue;  // SEAM: retry a zero-return forever
     }
-    zeros = 0;
     done += static_cast<std::size_t>(w);
   }
   return Status::Ok();
